property: comment <ME:0000011> = Soil test report of the University of Georgia Soil, Plant, and Water Laboratory (Athens, GA) for Sindhu Jagadamma, completed 2015-08-06; eight depth intervals of the FWB-306 core collected 2015-06-10, each analysed in duplicate
property: comment <ME:0000011> = Method Mehlich 1: elements extracted from the soil by the Mehlich 1 dilute acid solution. Method water extract: 5 g soil shaken in 20 mL deionized water for 15 minutes. All values are mg per kg of soil. Nitrate is reported as nitrate nitrogen
property: comment <ME:0000011> = A blank concentration is a value the laboratory reported as below its detection limit; every sample was measured for every analyte. The detection limit of each analyte is on the molecule dimension (blank for analytes that were always detected). For the Mehlich 1 elements it is the smallest limit in the report: the laboratory states a limit for each sample, and it differs between samples (Cd: 0.04, 0.05, 0.06; Cr: 0.04, 0.05; Mo: 0.04, 0.05, 0.06; Pb: 0.03, 0.05 mg/kg; for Cd, Cr and Mo the limit rises with the sample's moisture, which suggests a dry-soil basis)
property: comment <ME:0000011> = Below the detection limit in every sample (all concentrations blank): Cd (Mehlich 1; limit 0.04 to 0.06 mg/kg); Mo (Mehlich 1; limit 0.04 to 0.06 mg/kg); fluoride (water extract; limit 0.7 mg/kg); phosphate (water extract; limit 4 mg/kg); U (water extract; limit 1 mg/kg)
property: comment <ME:0000011> = Source: ENIGMA Google Drive, FRC Well Metadata/Core samples/FW306_Sediment_chemical analysis.xls. The ORNL FRC sample collection log carries a rounded copy of these values
